  "findings": [
    "session/set_config_option takes value as a plain string; the documented {\"value\": \"...\"} object is rejected (-32602, untagged enum SessionConfigOptionValue).",
    "The response is the complete option list, mirrored by a config_option_update session/update.",
    "Switching the model keeps the current reasoning_effort when the new model offers it (grok-4.7 low -> grok-4.5 low); a model without reasoning control has no reasoning_effort option, and setting one is refused (unknown reasoning_effort value).",
    "A value the model does not offer (xhigh or minimal on grok-4.5) is refused with -32602 unknown reasoning_effort value; the session keeps its value.",
    "Per-model effort lists and defaults are also in session/new models.availableModels[]._meta (supportsReasoningEffort, reasoningEffort, reasoningEfforts[].default).",
    "Model switches with set_config_option (no leader) write nothing to $GROK_HOME/config.toml: no default_model is persisted.",
    "grok 1.0.41 agent stdio removes $GROK_HOME/requirements.toml at startup and appends [marketplace] default_skills_installs_purged = true to config.toml (inspect --json still reports the lock before the agent starts)."
  ]
